p class=\"prf-lede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 8 grids in Pierce County has come in under 90% of normal in January to February in 38 of 75 years since 1951. In 2026 so far, the middle of the grids ran 56% of normal in May to June and 73% in April to May. A preliminary estimate puts July to August 2026 at 51.6 on grid 29551. Every grid had its driest year in 1976, with grid 29849 at 53%.</p>"}
